    {
      "name": "Site Navigation",
      "kind": "nav",
      "refersTo": "nav-link",
      "description": "Mauve aa monogram, pill links with a Mauve Tint current state, compact primary button.",
      "html": "<nav class=\"ds-nav\"><a class=\"ds-mark\" href=\"#\"><span class=\"ds-mono\">aa</span>Arya Aji Kusuma</a><a class=\"ds-link\" href=\"#\">Services</a><a class=\"ds-link\" aria-current=\"page\" href=\"#\">Work</a><a class=\"ds-link\" href=\"#\">Notes</a><a class=\"ds-cta\" href=\"#\">Start a project</a></nav>",
      "css": ".ds-nav{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:.15rem;padding:.6rem 1rem;background:var(--bg);border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);font-family:var(--font-body)}.ds-mark{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:.6rem;margin-right:auto;color:var(--heading);text-decoration:none;font-family:var(--font-display);font-weight:700}.ds-mono{display:grid;place-items:center;width:2.1rem;height:2.1rem;border-radius:50%;background:var(--accent);color:var(--on-accent);font-weight:760;letter-spacing:-.04em}.ds-link{padding:.45rem .75rem;border-radius:var(--r-chip);color:var(--text);text-decoration:none;font-weight:600}.ds-link:hover{background:var(--column);color:var(--heading)}.ds-link[aria-current=page]{background:var(--accent-tint);color:var(--accent)}.ds-link:focus-visible,.ds-cta:focus-visible{outline:3px solid var(--accent);outline-offset:3px}.ds-cta{margin-left:1rem;padding:.55em 1em;border-radius:var(--r-card);background:var(--accent);color:var(--on-accent);font-family:var(--font-display);font-weight:650;text-decoration:none}.ds-cta:hover{background:var(--accent-strong)}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Task Board",
    "overview": "**Creative North Star: \"The Task Board\"**\n\nThe whole site is one kanban board. A chore someone does by hand is a card; the work Arya sells is moving that card into the \"Automated\" column with a real estimate on it. Every recurring container on the site is built from the same three layers of a board: a Mantle board panel, Crust columns inside it, and raised paper cards inside those. Services are columns of the chores they absorb, the process is four columns with one card each, and project outcomes are written as chips, like due dates on a task.\n\nColour is Catppuccin, never hand-mixed: Latte in daylight, Mocha when the visitor's system is dark, switched only by `prefers-color-scheme` (there is no toggle). The palette carries meaning on the board: Peach marks work done by hand, Green marks automated work, Mauve is the one action and the person who moves the work, Blue is a link. Density is medium and calm: soft rounded containers, short card titles in a highly legible text face, and big, tight Bricolage titles above them.\n\nMotion is a single story beat. On the home board, after hydration, the three chores strike through in \"By hand\" and arrive one by one in \"Automated\". The page renders in its finished state without JavaScript and skips the play under reduced motion.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Board, column, card: three nested tonal layers do almost all the layout work.",
      "A coloured stripe on the top edge of a card is its label.",
      "Chips (pill shapes) carry every estimate, price, count and outcome.",
      "One mauve action per view; the \"aa\" monogram is the same mauve.",
      "Latte and Mocha are equal citizens; every role token has both values."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Label Stripe Rule",
        "body": "A card's colour lives in a 4-5px stripe on its top edge, painted into the background so it follows the corner. The card body stays neutral paper. Never flood a card with its label colour.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Two Flavours Rule",
        "body": "Every role token is defined for Latte and Mocha in `:root` and its `prefers-color-scheme: dark` block. A new colour is not finished until it has both values.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Meaning Rule",
        "body": "Peach is by hand, Green is automated, Mauve is the action. Don't use Peach or Green decoratively, and don't use Mauve for anything a visitor can't act on except the monogram and mover that stand for Arya.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Two Faces Rule",
        "body": "Bricolage for things you scan (titles, buttons, the monogram, step numbers); Atkinson for things you read, including card text. No third face outside code blocks.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Paper Only Rule",
        "body": "Boards and columns never cast shadows; they are flat tonal fields with at most a 1px line. Only the card layer lifts.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** build new sections from the board, column, card layers before inventing a new container.",
      "**Do** put estimates, prices, counts and outcomes in chips, and tie them to real numbers.",
      "**Do** label a card with a top stripe in its role colour (Peach by hand; Yellow, Green or Teal by kind of tool).",
      "**Do** define every new colour for both Latte and Mocha, taking values from the Catppuccin flavours.",
      "**Do** keep one solid mauve button per view, with any secondary action as a ghost button.",
      "**Do** render animated states in their finished form first and play motion only after hydration, never under reduced motion."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** add shadows to boards or columns; only cards lift.",
      "**Don't** fill a card with its label colour or use Peach or Green as decoration.",
      "**Don't** add a light/dark toggle or a third flavour; the system follows the visitor's setting.",
      "**Don't** set card text in Bricolage or add a third typeface.",
      "**Don't** reuse the green \"aa\" tile from the favicon, apple-touch icon and OG image. It predates this palette, and the system monogram is the mauve circle."
    ]
  }
